 incident but haven't rolled anything back yet. There's no service called just \"payments,\" and two payments services turned out to be failing, so I need you to tell me which one to roll back.\n\n**What I found** (both are failing in all three production regions, us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate):\n\n| Service | Current version | Status | Last healthy version in production |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| payments-api | v5.1.0 | degraded | v5.0.0 |\n| payments-worker | v3.4.0 | unhealthy | v3.3.0 |\n\nYou asked me to roll back one service. The deploy history doesn't have timestamps, so I can't tell which one was deployed this morning. Both having exactly the same error rate suggests one may be breaking the other. Rolling back the wrong service would change production for no reason, so I'd rather check with you first.\n\n**Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2) is open and has paged on-call. It's filed under payments-api, but the summary covers both services and says the rollback is waiting on this decision.\n\n**Which should I do?**\n1. Roll back payments-api to v5.0.0\n2. Roll back payments-worker to v3.3.0\n3. Roll back both\n\nBoth target versions were healthy in production before, so none of these needs change-manager approval. I can run whichever you pick straight away.", "type": "text"}]}]}